    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "The Constituent Assembly took 2 years, 11 months, and 18 days to frame the Constitution of India.",
        "Dr. B.R. Ambedkar chaired the Drafting Committee, which played a pivotal role in finalizing the text.",
        "The Constitution was formally adopted on November 26, 1949, and came into effect on January 26, 1950.",
        "The Objective Resolution moved by Jawaharlal Nehru in 1946 laid down the foundational principles of the Constitution."
      ],
      "id": "4ffg1pk"
    },
